Z||000000||tgowens||06-29-2000||10:40 AM||||I recently made a 2800 mile trip from CA to KY.......on the trip I saw two red notchbacks on a flatbed being towed by a blue pickup just north of Denver and a black notchback around Limon, CO ----- and believe it or not, that's all I saw on the road..........did these belong to a forum member?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-30-2000||03:44 PM||||In my drives from NYS to Florida and back, I didn't see one Fiero on the road until I got off the interstates near Daytona.<P>In my drive from NYS to Wisconsin, Kansas City and back I didn't see more than one Fiero on the highways.  I don't think that either my timing was right or few take their Fieros on the highways for cross country trips.<P>So the Fiero on the highway is a rare breed.  That why Fiero caravans look neat.||||reg||6
Z||000002||tgowens||06-30-2000||04:17 PM||||Old Lar, I agree, I have driven from OH/KY to CA three times since October and I have seen few on the road - most of them seem to be around the big cities and not too far out of the city either -- most of the 'daily drivers' tend to stay close to home....it's always a rare sight to see one and a treat too -- funny thing tho, they always seem to be going the opposite direction from me so I have yet to pull over and talk to a Fiero driver on any of my trips!!||||reg||1
